IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sea-employee`

-- Seafarers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1992 (Cth) -- the seat of the EMPLOYER, which under this Act is itself
-- liable to pay compensation and determines the claim (ss 24, 25). "By when must I decide this claim? Must I be insured?
-- By when must I reconsider? How much must I pay this week? How much for a permanent impairment?"
--
-- Every question calls a rule in sea-employee.l4 and restates none: the claim time limits (ss 72, 73, 73A), the weekly
-- amount (ss 31, 38), permanent impairment (s 39). The duties that are the employer's alone -- insurance (s 93) and the
-- reconsideration time limit (s 79) -- are encoded here.
--
-- Edition, scope and the caveats on lost formulas and indexed amounts: see sea-employee.l4 and NOTES.md. BASELINE. Not
-- for public use as advice.

§ `Seafarers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1992 -- the employer's questions`

§§ `ss 72, 73, 73A -- by when must I decide a claim`

@export By when must I determine my liability on a seafarer's claim, before it is taken to be disallowed (ss 72, 73, 73A)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Claim for the time limit` @desc What the claim is for
      `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the claim
      `I asked the claimant for information within the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within the 12 days (incapacity, property, medical), 60 days (death) or 30 days (permanent impairment), you asked the claimant by notice under s 67 for information, a document or an authority
      `the day I asked` IS A DATE @desc The day you asked (ignored if you did not)
      `the day I received what I asked for` IS A DATE @desc The day you received it (ignored if you did not ask)
      `the Authority allowed me a further period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on your written request, the Authority allowed you a further period by a notice served before your time ran out
      `the end of the further period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that further period (ignored if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I decide the claim` MEANS
    `the last day for the employer to determine the claim` `the claim` `the day I received the claim` `I asked the claimant for information within the period` `the day I asked` `the day I received what I asked for` `the Authority allowed me a further period` `the end of the further period`

§§ `s 79 -- by when must I reconsider` -- arises only if a claimant has asked for reconsideration

-- s 79(1): the employer "must reconsider the determination before the later of the following times: (a) the end of the
-- period of 60 days after the employer receives the request; (b) if ... the Authority ... allows a further period ...--the
-- end of that period". (2): increased by the days "after the day on which the request was made and before the day on which
-- the employer receives the information" asked for under s 83 within the period. (6): if not done, the employer "is taken
-- to have made a decision, at the end of that period, disallowing the claim". (The s 83A medical examination extension in
-- (3) is not encoded.)
@export By when must I reconsider a determination a claimant has asked me to reconsider (s 79)?
GIVEN `the day I received the request` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the claimant's request for reconsideration
      `I asked for information within the 60 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within the 60 days, you asked the claimant by notice under s 83 for information, a document or an authority
      `the day I asked` IS A DATE @desc The day you asked (ignored if you did not)
      `the day I received what I asked for` IS A DATE @desc The day you received it (ignored if you did not ask)
      `the Authority allowed me a further period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority allowed you a further period, by a notice served in time
      `the end of the further period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that further period (ignored if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I reconsider` MEANS
    IF `the Authority allowed me a further period` AND `the end of the further period` GREATER THAN `the statutory day`
    THEN `the end of the further period`
    ELSE `the statutory day`
    WHERE
        `the days of the request` MEANS
            IF `I asked for information within the 60 days`
            THEN max 0 (DATE_SERIAL `the day I received what I asked for` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the day I asked` MINUS 1)
            ELSE 0
        `the statutory day` MEANS `the day I received the request` PLUS (60 PLUS `the days of the request`)

§§ `s 93 -- must I be insured`

-- s 93(1): "an employer, other than the Fund, must on each day: (a) have a policy of insurance or indemnity from an
-- authorised insurer; or (b) be a member of a protection and indemnity association that ... is approved in writing by the
-- Authority; and ... is a member of the International Group of Protection and Indemnity Associations; or (c) be a member
-- of an employers' mutual indemnity association that is approved in writing by the Authority; so that the employer is
-- insured or indemnified for the full amount of the employer's liability under this Act to all employees". Penalty: 50
-- penalty units; (1A) strict liability.
DECLARE `Insurance` IS ONE OF
    `I comply: I am insured or indemnified for my full liability under the Act today (s 93(1))`
    `I am in breach: I must be insured or indemnified for my full liability every day; an offence of strict liability, up to 50 penalty units (s 93(1), (1A))`

@export Must I be insured against my liability under the Seafarers Act, and am I (s 93)?
GIVEN `I have an authorised insurer's policy or indemnity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a policy of insurance or indemnity from an authorised insurer
      `I am in an approved P&I club in the International Group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of a protection and indemnity association approved in writing by the Authority that is a member of the International Group of P&I Associations
      `I am in an approved employers' mutual indemnity association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of an employers' mutual indemnity association approved in writing by the Authority
      `it covers my full liability to all my employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that cover is for the full amount of your liability under the Act to all your employees (an excess the policy allows does not matter, s 93(2))
GIVETH AN `Insurance`
`Am I insured as the Act requires` MEANS
    IF     (`I have an authorised insurer's policy or indemnity` OR `I am in an approved P&I club in the International Group` OR `I am in an approved employers' mutual indemnity association`)
       AND `it covers my full liability to all my employees`
    THEN `I comply: I am insured or indemnified for my full liability under the Act today (s 93(1))`
    ELSE `I am in breach: I must be insured or indemnified for my full liability every day; an offence of strict liability, up to 50 penalty units (s 93(1), (1A))`

§§ `ss 31, 38, 39 -- what I must pay`

@export How much weekly compensation must I pay an incapacitated seafarer for this week (ss 31, 38)?
GIVEN `they are incapacitated for work this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of the injury, the employee cannot work at all this week, or not at the same rank or level
      `the weeks of incapacity before this one` IS A NUMBER @desc How many earlier weeks of incapacity count towards the first 45 (for a seafarer, after being left on shore at, or returned to, the home port)
      `their normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee's normal weekly earnings before the injury, in dollars
      `what they could earn this week in suitable employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What you determine (under s 32) the employee was able to earn this week in suitable employment, in dollars
      `the hours they were employed this week` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours the employee was employed this week
      `their normal weekly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee's normal weekly hours
      `they worked as a seafarer this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee was employed or engaged as a seafarer for any part of this week
      `AWOTE` IS A NUMBER @desc The Australian Statistician's Average Weekly Ordinary Time Earnings of full-time adults, in dollars
      `the minimum earnings base` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 31(9)(a) figure in force ($254.46 in this compilation, indexed)
      `the addition for a dependent prescribed person` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 31(10) figure in force ($62.99 in this compilation, indexed)
      `the addition for each prescribed child` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 31(11) figure per child in force ($31.50 in this compilation, indexed)
      `a prescribed person depends on them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a prescribed person is wholly or mainly dependent on the employee
      `the prescribed children who depend on them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many prescribed children are wholly or mainly dependent on the employee, not counting one counted as the prescribed person
      `they have reached pension age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee has reached pension age
      `they were injured within a year before pension age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee was injured at or after the age one year before pension age
      `the weeks already compensated` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of incapacity you have already compensated (counted only for an injury within a year before pension age)
      `they are imprisoned for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is in prison this week for an offence
GIVETH A `Weekly compensation`
`How much weekly compensation must I pay` MEANS
    `How much weekly compensation this week` `they are incapacitated for work this week` `the weeks of incapacity before this one` `their normal weekly earnings` `what they could earn this week in suitable employment` `the hours they were employed this week` `their normal weekly hours` `they worked as a seafarer this week` `AWOTE` `the minimum earnings base` `the addition for a dependent prescribed person` `the addition for each prescribed child` `a prescribed person depends on them` `the prescribed children who depend on them` `they have reached pension age` `they were injured within a year before pension age` `the weeks already compensated` `they are imprisoned for an offence`

@export How much permanent impairment compensation must I pay (s 39)?
GIVEN `it is the loss of a finger, toe, taste or smell` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the impairment is the loss, or loss of use, of a finger or toe, or the loss of taste or smell
      `the degree I determined` IS A NUMBER @desc The degree of permanent impairment you determined under the approved Guide, as a percentage
      `the maximum amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 39 maximum amount in force at the date of assessment ($100,778.56 in this compilation, indexed)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much permanent impairment compensation must I pay` MEANS
    `How much permanent impairment compensation under the Seafarers Act` `it is the loss of a finger, toe, taste or smell` `the degree I determined` `the maximum amount`
